      "instance_current_a": {
        "COMPARATOR": 0.00204341,
        "ADC_DECODE_BANK_P": 0.0151006,
        "ADC_DECODE_BANK_N": 0.0151006,
        "ADC_TOP_SW": 0.00213937
      },
      "_comment": "A peak is NOT additive: the deck measures i_vdd_peak_ua as the peak of the SUM (34383.9 uA), which is smaller than the sum of the three per-source peaks (39048.98 uA) because they do not peak at the same instant. Loading the three separate peaks would invent a worst case the deck never produces. The three per-source peaks are therefore scaled by 34383.9 / 39048.98 = 0.8805326029 so they sum to the measured peak-of-sum, preserving the attribution the deck measured while totalling what it measured. i_cdac_peak is split evenly between the two decode banks as above. This model drives the upper-bound case only."
    },
